// The page guide text in English (page -> { title, lead, blocks:[{h,p,ex,tip,demo}] }).
const HELP = {
  dash:{title:"About Home",lead:"Home is today's picture of your money: what you have, what came in and went out this month, and what is coming next. Everything here is for **this month** unless it says otherwise.",blocks:[
    {h:"What Home is for",p:["Home is a summary. Each box is a small version of another page, and the **All →** link on a box takes you to the full page.","A box only appears when it has something to show. On a brand new app you will see a short **Nothing here yet** card with two buttons: **Connect an account** and **Add a transaction**.","Hover over (or tap) most numbers to see how they were worked out."],ex:"No jars yet? The **Jars** box is simply not shown."},
    {h:"What is counted, and what is not",p:["**Upcoming bills** are predictions. They are not counted as spending or income and they do not change your balances or totals. Only a bill due this month and not yet paid reduces the **available** figure."]},
    {h:"Alerts at the top",p:["If something needs you, up to three alerts show in a yellow box above everything. Press **Open** to go to the thing the alert is about.","**All alerts (n) →** opens the full Alerts page."],demo:"alert",ex:"**Large income: Salary** for ₪18,900. Press **Open** and you see that payment in Activity."},
    {h:"The four big numbers",p:["**In your accounts** is the money you have in your bank and Wise right now, plus any account of your own that you chose to count. Credit cards are not included. A small line shows the total **With pension**.","**Money in** is all the money that came in this month so far, a cash deposit and your salary too. Money back (like a refund on a credit card) is not money in, and it does not lower money out: point at Money in to see it on its own line. **Money out** is what went out so far. **Saved this month (in − out)** is money in minus money out: what you kept.","Moving money between your own accounts, and paying a card bill from the bank, are not counted as income or spending."],demo:"kpis",ex:"You have ₪30,583 in your accounts. This month ₪18,900 came in and ₪10,013 went out, so **Saved this month** is ₪8,887."},
    {h:"Accounts and credit cards",p:["**Accounts** shows each bank, wallet and account of yours with its balance. A wallet with several currencies lists each one and what it is worth in shekels. Click an account to see its activity.","**Credit cards · upcoming vs last month** shows what you have spent on each card so far this month, next to last month. The small arrow says if you are spending more (up) or less (down). The bar is this month compared with last month.","Accounts you added by hand are shown slightly faded and are not clickable here."],demo:"account",ex:"Card **Max ·· 1234**: ₪3,200 so far, last month ₪2,900. You see **▲ 10%**."},
    {h:"Money flow · ahead",p:["This is a plan for the money you have right now, for the rest of this month. The first bar is **In your accounts**: the same number as the card at the top. Each bar after it takes a piece away: card purchases not paid yet, bills still due this month, what is **left in your budgets** this month (biggest first), then what is **put aside**: money in jars and the safety cushion.","After **Card purchases not paid yet** and **Bills still due this month** (bills not paid yet this month and payments already listed for a later day) you see **your money after known payments**: what is left once the amounts you already know about are paid.","Above each bar is its amount. In the block under each bar is **what is left** of your money after that item. For a budget or bill, the bar is only what is still left to spend in it this month, not what you already spent.","The **Current / Planned** switch changes the view. Both start from **In your accounts**. **Current** takes off only card purchases not paid yet and bills still due this month, so it ends at **Your money after known payments**: the money that is yours today. Jars, the cushion and what is left in your budgets are plans, so this view leaves them out. **Planned** also takes off what is left in your budgets this month and what is put aside, so it ends at **Free to use**.","The last bar is **Free to use** (green): money nothing needs. **Short** (red) means more is planned than you have."],demo:"waterfall",ex:"₪30,000 in accounts. ₪2,000 card purchases not paid yet and ₪1,000 of bills still due, so **your money after known payments** is ₪27,000. ₪7,000 left in your groceries budget. ₪10,000 put aside in jars. So **Free to use** is ₪10,000.",tip:"Only the 8 biggest bars show. The rest are joined into one bar called **Other**."},
    {h:"Left to spend vs whole month",p:["Switch the picture with the two buttons. **Left to spend** looks forward from today: each bar is only what you can still spend.","**Whole month** shows each budget in full. The filled part is what you already spent. The striped part is what is still to spend. The first bar becomes the money in your accounts plus what you already spent, so it shows what you had to work with this month."],ex:"Groceries budget ₪2,600, spent ₪900. **Left to spend** shows a ₪1,700 bar. **Whole month** shows a ₪2,600 bar, ₪900 filled and ₪1,700 striped.",tip:"**Full breakdown →** opens a window that lists every amount in the calculation. Money that a jar already pays for is not counted twice."},
    {h:"Spending and budgets",p:["**Spending by category** is a ring that shows where this month's spending went. Click a slice to see those payments.","**Budgets** shows your biggest budgets as bars. The thin line on each bar is today's date in the month. If the colour is past the line, you are spending faster than the month is passing."],demo:"budgetbar",ex:"Groceries ₪901 of ₪2,600 on day 10 of 30. The bar is about a third full and the line is also near a third, so you are on pace."},
    {h:"Bills, recent and jars",p:["**Upcoming bills** lists the next four bills. Overdue ones come first. A **≈** in front of an amount means the amount changes from month to month.","**Recent activity** shows your last five payments. Click one to open it.","**Jars** shows each jar's progress and how much it received this month. At the bottom, **Free to use** is the money that is free for jars right now."],demo:"bill",ex:"**Netflix** - Due 6 Nov, in 24 days - ₪55."},
    {h:"Exchange rates",p:["If you hold money in another currency (for example in Wise), this box shows its rate in shekels for the last 30 days, with the lowest, average and highest. Pick another currency with the buttons on top.","The rates come from the European Central Bank. They are only used to turn your foreign balances into shekels. **Currencies →** opens Settings."],ex:"€1 = ₪4.0000 today. Your €500 counts as ₪2,000 in your totals."}
  ]},

  tx:{title:"About Activity",lead:"Activity is the list of every payment that came in or went out, from all your accounts. Use it to look something up, fix a category, or add a note.",blocks:[
    {h:"What Activity is for",p:["Think of it as your bank statement, but for all accounts together. Newest is first.","Amounts in green came in. Amounts in black went out. If a payment was in another currency, the original amount is shown under the shekel amount."],ex:"₪48 at Pharmacy on 3 Oct, from Max ·· 1234, category Health."},
    {h:"Likely bills and upcoming rows",p:["Rows marked **likely bill** or **Upcoming** are predictions or future-dated items. They are shown so you can plan, but they are not counted in In, Out or Net, in reports, balances or budgets until they are paid."]},
    {h:"Two tabs",p:["**All activity** is the full list.","**Needs review** holds things the app is not sure about. The number in brackets is how many. See the block about review below."],demo:"tabs"},
    {h:"Search and filters",p:["The search box looks in the store name, your note and the tags. **Clear** resets every filter.","Next to it are drop-downs: **All sources** (which account), **All categories**, **All tags**, **All types** (Income, Salary, Money back, Expenses, Transfers, Card payments, Bills), and the date range. The date range starts as **All time**. Choose **Custom range…** to type two dates.","The last drop-down groups the list: by day, week, month, category, type, account, merchant or tag. Each group shows its own In, Out and Net, and you can click its title to fold it."],ex:"Choose **Groceries** and **This month**: you see only grocery payments from this month."},
    {h:"The totals strip",p:["Above the list: how many **Transactions** you see, and **In**, **Out** and **Net** for them.","The line under them, such as **451 transactions · 84 not in the totals**, says how many rows are shown but not added: transfers, card bill payments, upcoming payments, balance updates, and rows you left out. Point at it to see each reason with its number. This way nothing is counted twice.","Money back is not added to **In** and does not lower **Out**: when there is some, it shows as its own **Money back** total next to them."]},
    {h:"Reading a row",p:["Each row has the date, the store, **From → To** (which account the money left and where it went), the category, tags, the amount and a paperclip if you attached a receipt.","You can change the **Category** straight from the row. If the payment had no category, the app offers to make a rule so the next ones are sorted by themselves.","Small labels explain special rows: **bill**, **upcoming**, **expected bill**, **card payment**, **transfer**, **ignored**, **balance update**, **Jar · name**, and **3/10** for a payment in instalments (payment 3 of 10)."]},
    {h:"Money coming in",p:["Money coming in is **Income**, unless it came in on a credit card: that is **money back**. Nothing is decided from the words in it, so a bank deposit called \"זיכוי\" and a cash deposit are Income.","A small label shows **salary** or **money back**; point at it to see why (it came in on a credit card, your rule, or you marked it). Other income has no label.","Income counts as money in, salary too. Money back is its own total: it is not money in, and the purchase still counts in full. A card credit still lowers that card's bill.","Wrong kind? Open the payment and pick **Income**, **Salary** or **Money back** under **What is this money?**, or **Automatic** to let the app decide again. It is saved in the change history and can be undone. For every payment from the same payer, add a rule in Settings → Money coming in."],ex:"Your salary arrives as \"זיכוי\": it counts as Income. Mark it **Salary** once, or add a rule with the employer's name, and it shows as your salary."},
    {h:"Opening a payment",p:["Click the store name to open the payment. You can see every detail the bank sent, change the category, add tags and a note, and attach a receipt.","There are one-click tiles: **Mark as a bill** (the app starts to expect it), **Attach to a jar** (the payment came out of a jar), **Card payment** (it is a card bill, not spending) and **Count this one out** (leave it out of all totals).","Click the paperclip to view attached receipts or photos."],ex:"A ₪55 charge from Netflix: press **Mark as a bill** and it shows up in Bills."},
    {h:"Needs review",p:["**Transfers between your accounts**: the app thinks money moved from one of your accounts to another. Press **Confirm**, or **Not a transfer** if it was real spending or income. If a fee was taken, it is shown as a cost.","**Possible duplicates**: the same amount, store and day twice. Press **Delete this copy** or **Keep both**.","**Balance changes with no transaction**: the bank balance moved but no payment explains it. Choose **I know what it was** (add it), **Count it as a charge**, or **Leave it, with a note…**."],ex:"Wise balance dropped ₪200 with no payment: press **I know what it was**, type the store, pick a category."},
    {h:"Export and focus",p:["**Export…** downloads what you see, as a file. You can change the filters inside the window first.","Sometimes another page sends you here to look at a few specific payments. A box says **Showing only N items**. Press **Show all activity** to go back to the full list.","Long lists load 50 at a time. Press **Show 50 more** at the bottom."]}
  ]},

  acc:{title:"About Accounts",lead:"This page lists every account the app knows about: the ones it reads from your bank and cards, and any you add yourself. Open one to see its balance, charts and its own activity.",blocks:[
    {h:"What Accounts is for",p:["The app only shows connected accounts after you connect them in **Settings → Connections** or import a file. Until then, this page is empty.","Accounts are grouped as **Bank accounts**, **Credit cards**, **Wallets** and **Other accounts** (the ones you enter by hand, plus your pension)."],demo:"account",ex:"Bank Hapoalim, balance ₪23,840, **Connected**, 123 transactions."},
    {h:"Account cards",p:["Each card shows the name, the type, the balance and a status badge. A credit card shows what was charged this month and last month instead of a balance. A number like **ending 1234** is the last digits.","If one login has several cards, you get one account per card, for example **Max ·· 1234** and **Max ·· 5678**."]},
    {h:"What the status means",p:["**Connected**: it synced fine. **Out of date**: it has not synced for a while. **Needs a code**: the bank wants a one-time code. **Locked**: the app paused it after two failed logins. **Entered by you**: you keep this balance by hand.","The app can only read. It can never move money."],demo:"status"},
    {h:"Add your own account",p:["Press **+ Add an account** for something with no connection: cash, savings at another place, an investment, or a loan.","Fill in a **Name**, a **Type**, a **Currency** and the **Balance now**. For a loan or debt, type what you owe as a minus number.","Two options: **Count it in my net worth** adds the balance to your net worth (never to the cash that jars use). **Count its transactions in reports** puts its income and spending into reports, budgets and the forecast. Turn that off if you only want to watch the balance."],ex:"Savings at Meitav, ₪15,000, counted in net worth, not counted in reports."},
    {h:"Updating a balance by hand",p:["On your own account page press **Update balance**, type the new balance and an optional note. The old balance is not lost: it is kept in the **Balance history** list.","In **Activity** each update appears as a **balance update** note. It is never counted as income or spending."],ex:"Cash was ₪1,000, now ₪800: balance update of −₪200. Your reports do not change."},
    {h:"One account page",p:["Click any card. At the top: **← All accounts**, **+ Add a transaction**, and buttons that fit the account. Your own accounts have **Update balance**, **Edit** and **Remove**. A connected one has **Go to connection →**.","Below you see tiles: current balance and this month's **In**, **Out** and **Net** (a card shows **Charged this month**, **Last month**, and the balance the card reports), plus the last 12 months and the number of transactions.","The chart shows the balance over 12 months, worked out backwards from today's balance and the payments. For your own accounts it shows every time you updated it. For a card it shows what was charged each month."]},
    {h:"Details and activity",p:["**Account details** tells you the type, currency, provider, connection state, when the balance last updated, and if the account is counted in net worth and in reports.","Cards are not counted in net worth, because a card is a bill, not money you have.","The activity list below only shows this account. Use **Search this account…** to find a payment, or **Open in Activity →** to use all the filters."]},
    {h:"Pension",p:["The pension is hidden until it has a value. Set it with **Update balance** on its page, or in **Settings → Import and export**. You update it by hand.","It only counts in net worth when you switch on **Include pension** in Reports."]}
  ]},

  jars:{title:"About Jars",lead:"A jar is a pot of money inside this app, for a goal or for something you will need later. Jars do not move any real money in your bank. They just remind you what is spoken for.",blocks:[
    {h:"What jars are for",p:["Your bank shows one big number. Jars let you say: this part is for the summer trip, this part is for emergencies.","The money stays in your account. Jars fill from your **free** money, in order, so you never put aside money you do not really have."],ex:"Account ₪30,000. Jar Summer trip holds ₪4,000. You still have ₪26,000 that is not set aside."},
    {h:"Free to use",p:["The big number on the left is your free money: what no bill, no budget and no jar needs.","It is your accounts, minus card purchases not paid yet, minus bills still due this month, minus what is left in your budgets, minus what is put aside (jars and the amount you keep untouched).","Income still to come, like your salary, counts only once it arrives, so before payday this can be below zero.","**How is this worked out?** opens a list of every piece."],ex:"₪30,000 in accounts - ₪2,000 upcoming payments - ₪3,000 left in budgets - ₪15,000 put aside = ₪10,000 free to use.",tip:"If you see **too much** in red, your jars and cushion add up to more than you have. Nothing is taken from a jar by itself. Jars stop filling. **Take ₪X back from the jars** frees the difference."},
    {h:"Put into jars this month",p:["This box shows how much the jars received this month, out of how much they wanted. The bar fills as they receive money.","**Put in so far** is what they got. **Still to put in** is what they still need. **Available now** is the free money you could use for it. If it is zero, jars wait until more money is free."],ex:"₪800 of ₪1,200 put in. ₪400 still to put in. ₪0 available: the jars wait."},
    {h:"Keep untouched",p:["This is your cushion: money the jars never use. Pick **None**, ₪1,000, ₪2,000, ₪5,000 or ₪10,000, or type another amount."],ex:"Keep ₪5,000 untouched for emergencies. Jars will only fill from money above that."},
    {h:"Your jars, in priority order",p:["Each month the jars take free money in order. Jar number 1 gets it first. Change the order with the arrows or the number box on the jar.","A jar with a goal and a monthly amount takes that monthly amount. A jar with a goal but no monthly amount takes everything it can, up to its goal, before the next jar gets anything. A jar with no goal and no monthly amount takes nothing by itself.","**Fill now** fills the jars right away from the free money. Without pressing it, jars also fill as free money comes in."],demo:"jar",ex:"Summer trip: ₪4,000 of ₪20,000 (20%), ₪800 a month, **Full by** a date the app works out."},
    {h:"Reading a jar card",p:["The ring shows how full the jar is. **Saved** is what it holds. **Goal** is the target. **Monthly** is the amount per month, or **Top-up** if it just takes what it can. **Full by** is the month it should be full.","The pill at the top shows this month's state: **Funded**, **Partly funded**, **Needs ₪X**, **Full** or **No auto-fill**. Click it to see the jar's history of money in and out.","The **⋯** menu has **Edit jar**, **Mark as done** and **Delete jar**."],tip:"**Full by** is honest. It uses the free money you have now plus the surplus the Forecast expects each month, the same as the Forecast page."},
    {h:"New jar and goals",p:["**+ New jar** asks: what is it for? **Savings** (money for something: a goal and a date are optional, and you can set an amount per month), **Bills** (keep money for your bills, for the months you choose) or **Pay-off** (a loan you pay back: the total you owe, what you already paid back, and what you pay each month).","A **Pay-off** jar counts up. When you pay the loan, the jar does not go down: it shows how much you have paid back. Money you already paid back, and savings you tick as **not in my accounts here**, never reduce your free money, because that money is not in your accounts","You can also tick **Pays for these categories**. Spending in those categories then comes out of the jar by itself.","The **Goals** list shows jars that have a goal, with a state: **On track**, **Behind**, **Saving**, **Reached** or **No monthly amount**. **Raise to ₪X a month** fixes a jar that is behind. **Mark as done** closes a reached goal."],ex:"Pays for **Shopping**: a ₪120 lamp lowers the jar by ₪120."},
    {h:"Completed jars",p:["Finished jars move to **Completed jars**. Press **History** to see what was paid, or **Reopen** to use the jar again."]}
  ]},

  bills:{title:"About Bills",lead:"Bills are payments you expect to see again, like rent, phone or Netflix. This page finds them for you, predicts the next one and warns you when something looks wrong.",blocks:[
    {h:"What Bills is for",p:["The app watches your payments. When the same store charges you again and again, it becomes a bill and the next payment is predicted.","The category does not matter. Car insurance is a bill whatever its category."],demo:"bill",ex:"Netflix charges ₪55 on the 6th every month. The app expects the next one on 6 Nov."},
    {h:"What is counted, and what is not",p:["Predicted and upcoming bills are **information only**. They are not added to your spending or income, they do not change any balance or report, and they do not use up a budget. A bill counts as spending only once it has actually been paid.", "The one place they matter is the **available** figure on Budgets: bills due **this month** that are not paid yet (and overdue ones) are held back from it, so you do not spend money that is already spoken for. Bills due next month are shown here but held back from nothing yet."]},
    {h:"The three numbers on top",p:["**Monthly total** is what your bills cost per month on average. Yearly bills are spread over 12 months. The small line also shows the yearly total.","**Due in the next 14 days** adds up the bills coming soon, using predicted amounts.","**Price changes** shows how much more (or less) you pay per year because some bills changed price."],ex:"Netflix went from ₪55 to ₪60. That is +₪5 a month, so **Price changes** shows ₪60 a year."},
    {h:"Four kinds of bills",p:["**Recurring**: same store, regular schedule (every month, every 2 months or every year). Found automatically.","**Irregular**: the timing varies, but you said every payment to that store is a bill, like a water bill.","**Instalments**: purchases you pay in parts, such as payment 3 of 10, with how many are left.","**One-off**: a single payment you marked as a bill."]},
    {h:"Reading a bill row",p:["Each row has the name, how often, which account pays, and the last charge. **Found automatically** or **Added by you** tells you how it got here. Hover over it to see the payments it was based on.","On the right is the amount. **≈** means the amount changes, and it is the average of the last 3. Under it: **Next 6 Nov**, **Due in 3 days**, **Due now**, or **Overdue since** a date.","A badge such as **▲ ₪5 more** tells you the price changed."]},
    {h:"The ⋯ menu",p:["**History** shows past payments. **Change type** switches between recurring and irregular.","**Mark to cancel** puts a **To cancel** badge on a subscription you plan to stop. Later choose **Mark as canceled**, or **Keep this bill**.","**Remove from bills** stops tracking it."],tip:"Canceled bills go to the **Canceled** list at the bottom. They are not counted in totals, predictions or alerts. **Restore** brings one back."},
    {h:"Add a bill yourself",p:["Press **+ Add bill** if a bill has not been charged yet, or its timing varies.","Fill the **Name**, **Expected amount**, **How often**, **Day of month**, **Paid from**, and optionally the text to match. Every payment containing that text counts as this bill. It defaults to the name."],ex:"Name Gym, ₪250, monthly, day 5."},
    {h:"Other ways to make a bill",p:["Open any payment in Activity and press **Mark as a bill**. Bills carry a **Bill** label in Activity.","A yearly bill needs two years of history to be found, or add it yourself."]}
  ]},

  budg:{title:"About Budgets",lead:"A budget is a limit for one category for one month, like Groceries ₪2,600. This page shows how you are doing against each limit, and helps you choose sensible limits.",blocks:[
    {h:"What budgets are for",p:["Budgets answer one question: am I spending too fast on this? Each budget starts again on the 1st of the month.","A bill that sits in the category is part of its budget. You do not need to count it twice."],demo:"budgetbar",ex:"Groceries budget ₪2,600. You spent ₪901 so far."},
    {h:"What is counted, and what is not",p:["A budget's **spent** amount counts only payments that really happened. Predicted bills never count as spent.", "The **available** figure also holds back the bills due **this month** that are not paid yet (and overdue ones), so it shows what is truly free. Bills due next month, and bills already covered by a jar, are not held back."]},
    {h:"The numbers on top",p:["**Left to spend** is what remains of all your budgets this month, with about how much that is per day for the rest of the month.","**Spent so far** is what you spent in those categories, out of all budgets added up. The thin line on its bar is today. Under it: the percent of the budget used and the percent of the month passed.","**Budgeted this month** is all limits added up. **Budgets** is how many you have: each budget is one category."],ex:"₪5,000 budgeted, ₪2,000 spent: ₪3,000 left. With 15 days to go that is ₪200 per day."},
    {h:"One budget card",p:["Each card shows the category, the status badge, what you spent of the limit, and a bar. The thin line on the bar is today. If the colour reaches past it, you are spending faster than time passes.","Under the bar: what is left, how much per day, and **at this pace you will spend** a guess for the whole month.","Next to the amount, three small bars show what you spent in the last three full months, with a word: **Going up**, **Going down** or **Steady**. It compares the last full month with the months before it. A change smaller than 10% (or than ₪50) counts as steady. Point at it to see each month's amount. Months over the limit are red."],ex:"₪400, ₪400, then ₪520: the last month is ₪120 more than before, so it says **Going up**."},
    {h:"What the badges mean",p:["**Within budget**: you are fine and on pace to stay inside.","**Likely to go over**: fine today, but at this pace you will pass the limit before the month ends.","**Almost at the limit**: you used 80% or more. You can change that percent in Settings → Which alerts.","**Over by ₪X**: you already spent more than the budget."],ex:"Limit ₪2,600, spent ₪901 on day 10 of 30. Pace: ₪2,703. Badge: **Likely to go over**."},
    {h:"Extras on a card",p:["**Includes bills** opens the list of bills in that category. **Paid from a jar** shows when a jar pays for spending here.","The **⋯** button on a card has **Change amount**, **Show in Activity** and **Remove budget**. Remove asks first, and your payments are not touched."]},
    {h:"Suggested budgets",p:["After two full months of history, the app suggests budgets from what you really spent, plus about 5% room. Categories that are mostly bills are left out.","Change the amount if you like and press **Accept**. **Accept all** takes all of them. **Not this one** hides a suggestion. **Show dismissed suggestions again** brings them back. Nothing is created until you accept."],ex:"You spent ₪2,300, ₪2,500 and ₪2,400 on Groceries. Suggested budget: ₪2,550."},
    {h:"Raise or lower hints",p:["Sometimes a card shows a question: you went over in 2 of the last 3 months, raise it? Or you spend far under the limit, lower it?","Press **Use ₪X** to apply, or **Not now**."]},
    {h:"Spending with no budget",p:["Below, **Spending with no budget** lists categories you spend in that have no limit. **Set budget** makes one.","**+ Add budget** lets you choose a category and a monthly limit by hand. The form suggests an average of your last months."]}
  ]},

  rep:{title:"About Reports",lead:"Reports show how your money moves over time: net worth, income, spending, categories, stores and tags. Use it when you want to understand the past, not to plan the future.",blocks:[
    {h:"What Reports is for",p:["Every chart is built from your payments, month by month. Transfers between your own accounts, card bill payments and anything you left out are not included.","**Income** is all the money that came in, salary too. Money back is not income and does not lower spending. The same numbers show on Home.","The current month counts up to today only."],ex:"October shows spending up to today, not a full month."},
    {h:"The main chart",p:["The first drop-down chooses what to look at: **Net worth**, **Income**, **Expenses**, **Net cash flow (income − expenses)**, **Bills**, one **category**, one **income source** or one **tag**.","Next to it, **3M**, **6M**, **12M**, **3Y** and **All** choose how far back. The big number is the total, or for net worth, today's value with the change since the start.","Below the chart you see a small summary: total or now, monthly average or change, highest and lowest month. Click a point on the chart to see those payments in Activity."],demo:"forecast",ex:"Pick **Groceries** and **6M**: you see 6 bars or points, one per month, and the average month."},
    {h:"Chart style and options",p:["**Area**, **Line** and **Bars** change only how it looks. The numbers are the same.","The **Compare with the previous …** switch draws the period just before it, so you can see if you are doing better.","**Include pension** (only for net worth) adds your pension, which you update by hand. Without it, net worth is just cash and your own accounts counted in net worth.","**About this chart** explains what the chart includes."],ex:"Net worth, 12M, compare on: you see this year's line and last year's line."},
    {h:"This month vs last month",p:["This card compares your spending so far this month with the same day last month. Each category has two bars: this month on top, last month below.","The right side says how much of last month's full total you already spent."],ex:"On the 10th you spent ₪3,000. Last month by the 10th you spent ₪2,500. You are ▲ 20% higher."},
    {h:"Spending by category",p:["A ring that shows where spending went. Click a slice or a name to see those payments.","Pick a **time frame** in the drop-down above (today, this week, this month, last 30 days, this year, custom). The second drop-down can compare it with **the period before** or **the same dates last year**.","When comparing, you see a small table: this period, before, and the change."],demo:"donut"},
    {h:"Income vs expenses",p:["Green bars are income, the other colour is spending, for each month. Choose how many months to show, from the last 3 up to all history.","Click a bar to see that month's payments."]},
    {h:"Category trend",p:["Lines for your five biggest categories over time. Use the first drop-down to switch between **Expenses** and **Income**.","Hover over a dot to see its number. Click a dot to see that month's payments."]},
    {h:"Top merchants and tags",p:["**Top merchants** shows the 7 stores where you spent most. Click a name to see all payments there. Press **✕** if it is not a real store (a landlord or a card company). It is hidden and appears in **Hidden from this list**, where you can bring it back.","**Spending by tag** adds up spending per tag, like #vacation. Both use their own time frame and comparison."],demo:"tags"}
  ]},

  fc:{title:"About Forecast",lead:"Forecast guesses how much money will really be yours at the end of each month, for the next year, after paying for everything you bought. It starts from what is really yours at the end of this month and carries on your recent habits. It is not a promise.",blocks:[
    {h:"What Forecast is for",p:["It answers: if I keep living like this, how much will I have in 3 months, in 6 months, in a year? Will I ever go below zero?","There is no AI and no magic. It looks at your last few months and carries them forward, one month at a time."],demo:"forecast",ex:"Each month ₪18,000 comes in and ₪15,000 goes out, so you keep ₪3,000. From ₪30,000 you reach about ₪39,000 in 3 months."},
    {h:"The choice on top",p:["The chart always looks one year ahead. Each point is your balance on the last day of a month, starting with this month.","**Based on the last**: how many months it learns from: 3 (the usual), 6 or 12. 3 notices new changes fast. 12 also sees yearly costs, like holidays, but is slow to notice a new salary."]},
    {h:"The forecast's rules",p:["1. **Months:** it learns from exactly the number of months you chose (3, 6 or 12): this month and the months just before it. The same months for every row, income and spending, on any day of the month. No other months are used.","2. **This month** = what really happened up to today + what usually happens after today's date. If something usually paid later in the month was already paid earlier this month, it is not added again. A salary that usually comes later in the month and has not come yet counts as coming.","3. **What usually happens after today** is learned from the 2 full months before this month (always those 2), from the real payment dates, payee by payee, and from your known bills still due.","4. **Average** (per month) = the plain average of the months shown. A month with nothing counts as ₪0. **Income** is expected to be exactly its average every month. For **spending**, a very unusual month is first pulled toward normal.","5. **Spending counts in the month you buy**, card purchases too. The forecast starts from **the money you'll likely have** at the end of this month: the balance likely then, less this month's card purchases not paid yet. Each month after that = the month before + money in − money out.","6. **Trend:** if a spending row is going up or down, that fades within a few months and never goes more than 20% away from the average. An income row shows its trend only for information.","7. **Only in one month:** a row with money in only one of the months shown is expected to be its average every month.","8. **Jars and alerts** use the same forecast, from the same months you chose."],ex:"It is October 20. Rent of ₪4,000 was paid on the 5th: October counts ₪4,000. Fuel of ₪600 usually comes on the 25th and ₪100 was paid so far: October counts ₪600."},
    {h:"Where it starts",p:["The first step is the end of this month: today's balance, less the bills and card charges still due this month, less what usually still goes out after today, plus income still expected this month (rules 2 and 3). Then it takes off this month's card purchases not paid yet: what is left is **the money you'll likely have** on the last day of the month."],ex:"₪20,000 today, ₪3,000 of bills still to pay, ₪1,000 usually still spent after today and a ₪8,000 salary still to come: about ₪24,000 at the end of the month."},
    {h:"How each month is worked out",p:["Each month: the money you'll likely have at the end of the month before, plus the money that comes in, minus the money that goes out (card purchases count in the month you buy).","Each income is shown with the name you gave it, or else who sent it, or else its category. An income that came only in some months counts as its average over all the months (rule 4).","**Spending** is worked out for each category, the same way."],ex:"₪16,800 came in September and October, 2 of the last 3 months: it counts as ₪11,200 a month. Your card purchases in October are paid in November, but they are already taken off on October 31, so every month just adds what it saves."},
    {h:"What this is based on",p:["The months heading of the table (for example **Aug – Oct**) names the months used.","Card bill payments from your bank are not counted as spending, because the purchases are already counted on the card.","A red note appears if a month had no income. Then your history may be missing something. Try **Import history** in Settings → Connections."]},
    {h:"Four balance cards",p:["**End of** this month, **In 3 months**, **In 6 months** and **In 1 year**. Every number is **the money you'll likely have** then: your balance after paying for everything you already bought (card purchases not paid yet and payments already due are taken off). The first card is the likely amount on the last day of this month, after the bills due and the usual spending still to come; in small, how much is in your bank today. The others show the change from the end of this month and where it will **probably** be.","The further ahead, the wider that range, because the future is less sure."],ex:"In 6 months: ₪48,000, ▲ ₪18,000, probably between ₪44,000 and ₪52,000."},
    {h:"The chart",p:["The line is the money you'll likely have. The shaded area (**Likely range**) is where it will probably be. Move over the chart to see a month's number.","The band shows how much your monthly result (money in − money out) changed from month to month in the months you chose. If your months are alike, for example ₪10,000 comes in every month and spending stays about the same, the band is narrow. If they differ a lot, for example a big payment in some months and almost nothing in others, the band is wide. It widens further ahead, because later months are harder to predict.","A badge tells the story: **Stays positive across the whole range**, **May dip below zero around** a month, or **Projected balance turns negative in** a month. The dashed red line is zero."]},
    {h:"What drives the forecast",p:["A table of money coming in and money going out. Each row has small bars, one per month it learns from, oldest first. This month's bar is striped: the solid part happened so far, the striped part usually still happens after today. Hover over a bar to see its month and amount, or tap the row's bars to see every month's exact amount.","Then: **Average** (per month), **Likely** (next month; income: its average; spending: the average, adjusted only if the row is going up or down), **Total** (next 12 months) and **Trend** (going up, going down or steady; **—** when the row had money in only one of the months, too little to tell). Hover over a column head to see what it means.","At the bottom: **Saved each month (money in − money out)** and **Money you'll likely have at month's end**: your money at the end of next month, and after 12 months, the same numbers as the chart.","Click a name to see its payments."],ex:"Groceries, with bars for Aug, Sep and Oct: ₪3,000, ₪3,000, and ₪2,000 so far (normally ₪3,000). **Average** ₪3,000 per month."},
    {h:"Jar forecast",p:["For every jar, a small chart shows how much it will hold over time and when it will be **Full**. It can only use money that is really free: the free money today plus what each month adds in the forecast, shared by priority. It uses the same months as the main chart.","Bill jars are expected to stay full. If it says **after the deadline** or **Not within 5 years**, the jar needs more money or more time. The dashed line is the goal."],demo:"jar",ex:"A summer trip needs ₪16,000 more, and free money grows by ₪1,000 a month: full in about 16 months."},
    {h:"Years ahead",p:["At the bottom of the Forecast page: what your money could add up to over many years. It starts from **In your accounts** (the same as on Home, without the pension) and adds **your average**: what came in minus what went out in each of the last full months, averaged. This month is not counted until it is over, and neither are transfers between your own accounts, card bill payments (the purchases are counted), upcoming payments or rows you left out. How many months: the choice in **Based on the last** at the top of the Forecast page.","Three boxes always follow the four choices (**Your goal**, **Set aside each month**, **By age** and **Growth each year**): **By age** (what you'll have by then), **Reaching** your goal (at about what age) and **Needed by age** (what to set aside each month to get there in time). Point at a box's name to see how it is worked out. Your average is shown under **Set aside each month**; when the amount differs from it, the **Reaching** box says how much sooner or later, the chart shows your average as a dashed line, and **Back to my average**, at the end of the **Set aside each month** heading, puts it back. Amounts and the age can be typed in their boxes or set with the sliders. The **Set aside each month** slider goes from ₪0 to a round amount based only on your average, so it stays the same when the age or the goal changes; a larger amount can still be typed.","With your **age** from Settings → Profile, the boxes say an age (**By age 50: ₪616,000**), up to age 100. Without it, they count in years from today. Nothing is saved to your data; the last choices are remembered for next time.","**Growth each year** is only a guess. 0% means the money doesn't grow: it stays the same, like money in a regular bank account. 3% is about what slow, safe saving might give, like a savings plan or a fixed deposit at the bank; 5% is about what money invested for many years might give, like a pension fund, a study fund or stocks. Real growth can be more, less, or the money can even go down. Each month gets its share of the yearly growth, so 12 months together grow by exactly that much."],ex:"₪40,000 in your accounts, ₪3,000 kept a month on average, age 34, goal ₪1,000,000 by 50: with no growth you'd have about ₪616,000 by 50 and reach the goal at about 61; to get there by 50 you'd need about ₪5,000 a month."},
    {h:"What is left out",p:["The pension is not in the forecast. A one-time cost, like a trip, only counts if it happened in the months the forecast learns from. Then it is spread evenly over every month: a one-time ₪955 in 3 months counts as ₪318 each month. The forecast is not advice."]}
  ]},

  alerts:{title:"About Alerts",lead:"Alerts are short messages about things that may need you: a bill due, a budget at its limit, a payment that looks strange. They tell you what to look at, they do not change anything.",blocks:[
    {h:"What alerts are for",p:["The app checks your data and shows an alert when something needs a look. The small bell number is how many are showing now.","Up to three also appear at the top of Home."],demo:"alert"},
    {h:"Two tabs",p:["**Alerts** shows what needs attention right now.","**History** shows every alert that ever appeared, when it appeared, and when it went away."],demo:"tabs"},
    {h:"Reading an alert",p:["The coloured dot shows how urgent it is. Then a title, a short line with the numbers, and two buttons.","**Open** takes you to the right place (the bill, the budget, the payment). **Dismiss** hides it. A dismissed alert does not come back, unless it is a new one."],ex:"**Netflix is due in 2 days** - About ₪55. Press **Open** to see the bill."},
    {h:"Kinds of alerts",p:["Bills due soon or overdue, bill price changes, budgets almost used or over, a card charge much higher than last month, a large payment, transfers and duplicates to review, a balance that changed with no payment to explain it, a source that is out of date, uncategorized payments, a forecast that goes below zero, income without a document, a jar that ran out, and payments that look like they came from a jar.","Each kind can be turned on or off, and some have limits you can change."]},
    {h:"History tab",p:["Each line shows **Active**, **Resolved** (the problem went away by itself) or **Dismissed** (you hid it). You also see when it appeared and how long it lasted.","Press **Show more** to go further back."],ex:"Appeared 3 Oct, 09:00 - gone 5 Oct, 18:00 (2 days)."},
    {h:"Change what you get",p:["**Alert settings →** opens Settings → Which alerts, where you choose the kinds and the limits.","Where alerts are sent (your phone, Telegram and so on) is set in Settings → Where alerts go."]}
  ]},

  cats:{title:"About Categories",lead:"A category is a label for a payment, like Groceries or Rent. Categories make your charts, budgets and forecast meaningful.",blocks:[
    {h:"What this page is for",p:["See where your money goes, per category and per tag. Two tabs: **Categories** and **Tags**.","Categories are the main label, one per payment. Tags are extra labels, as many as you want.","The rules that sort payments for you are in **Settings → Sorting**. **Go to category rules** and **Go to tag rules** take you there."],demo:"tabs"},
    {h:"Each row",p:["Choose **3, 6 or 12 months** at the top. Only full months count.","Each row shows the money that went out, the money that came in, in minus out, and a **usual month** (the average per month). It also says how this compares with the same number of months before.","Money moved between your own accounts and card bill payments are not counted, the same as in Reports.","Press a row to see its latest payments and a small chart, month by month. **See all in Activity** shows every payment in it."],ex:"Groceries: ₪1,500 out in 6 months, usual month ₪250, ₪120 less than the 6 months before."},
    {h:"Add, rename or delete",p:["Type a name and press **Add category** to make a new one.","The **⋯** button on a row renames it (if the new name exists, the two merge) or deletes it. Deleting never deletes payments.","Tags show here once a payment has one. You add them on a payment or with a tag rule."]},
    {h:"Where tags and categories are used",p:["Pick them in **Activity** (filter and group), in **Reports** (spending by category and by tag), and in **Budgets**. A payment can also get a tag or category when you open it."]}
  ]},

  "set.conn":{title:"About Connections",lead:"Here you connect your banks, cards and Wise so the app can read your payments by itself. The app is read-only: it can look, but it cannot move money.",blocks:[
    {h:"What this tab is for",p:["Add each bank or card you use. Only the ones you add are shown and synced.","Your logins are saved encrypted and are never shown again. Two failed logins pause a source, so the bank does not lock you."],demo:"status"},
    {h:"Add a connection",p:["Choose a bank, card or wallet in the list and press **Add**. A card appears with fields for your login, a **Nickname** (optional) and **Save**.","If a connection is not on the list, import a file from your bank instead in Settings → Import and export."],ex:"Choose **Max**, type your login, press **Save**."},
    {h:"Two logins at one company",p:["Have two Wise accounts, or two sets of cards? Pick the same company again from the list (it says \"another login\") and give each a nickname so you can tell them apart. The nickname is required for the second one."],ex:"Wise · Business and Wise · Personal."},
    {h:"A connected card",p:["Once connected, the card only shows the status and details: **Status**, **Last synced**, **Login verification** and **Accounts found** with their balances. **Login verification** shows the day it was done, or the day of the first sync that worked.","**Sync now** reads that connection right away. **Edit connection** opens the settings (and **Hide settings** closes them)."]},
    {h:"Inside Edit connection",p:["**Nickname** and the login fields. Saved logins show as \"saved - type to replace\". **Save** stores changes.","**Verify login** is for banks that ask for a one-time code. It opens the app's own browser, shown live: log in, type the code, tick \"remember this device\", and press **Done**. The bank then knows this browser, so automatic syncs should not ask again. Wise does not need it.","**Test connection** checks the login without saving anything. **Unlock** appears if the source was paused. **Remove** disconnects it."],tip:"Wise: create a personal token with read-only permissions."},
    {h:"Reading further back",p:["Beside **Sync now** on a connected card is how far back it reads. The first choice is the usual sync (the period set in Automatic sync, for example **Last 30 days**).","Pick **1 year**, **2 years** or **5 years** and press **Sync now** to read further back, once. The app keeps whatever the bank still has. Nothing already in the app is added twice. Then it goes back to the usual period."],ex:"You connected today and only have 1 year. Pick **5 years** and press **Sync now** to get older payments."},
    {h:"Statuses",p:["**Connected**, **Out of date**, **Last attempt failed**, **Locked**, **Needs a code**, **Not tested**, **No credentials**. If a source has a problem, a red line explains it."]}
  ]},

  "set.sync":{title:"About automatic sync",lead:"Sync is how the app fetches new payments and balances from your connections. This tab sets when it happens and shows a log of every sync.",blocks:[
    {h:"What sync is for",p:["The server syncs by itself, even when the app is closed. Opening the app never starts a sync.","You can always press **Sync now** (here, in Connections, or in the + menu)."],demo:"sync"},
    {h:"How often",p:["Choose **Once a day**, **Twice a day**, **Every 8 hours**, **Every 6 hours**, **Every 4 hours**, or **Never, only when I press Sync now**.","Then set the **Time of day** (or **First sync at**). Below it you see when the next sync will happen and when the last automatic one ran."],ex:"Every 8 hours, first at 06:00: syncs at 06:00, 14:00 and 22:00."},
    {h:"How far back each sync reads",p:["**Each routine sync reads the last** 2 weeks, 30 days, 60 days or 90 days. Shorter is quicker and gentler on the bank.","**First import of a new source reads** 3 months up to 5 years. It is used once when you connect. The bank decides how much it still keeps, usually 1 to 2 years."],ex:"Routine sync of 30 days: each time, the last 30 days are checked and new payments added. Old ones are not duplicated."},
    {h:"Past syncs",p:["Under the settings: every sync, with the connection name, **Succeeded**, **Failed** or **Running**, when it ran, **Automatic** or **Manual**, and how long it took.","**Asked for** is the period requested. **Returned** is how many transactions came back and how far back they go. **New** is how many were new to the app. A failure shows the reason."],tip:"Press **Refresh** to update the list, or **Show 50 more** at the bottom."},
    {h:"If something fails",p:["A failed line shows the reason right under it. A bank asking for a code needs **Verify login** in Connections. A locked source needs a check of the login, then **Unlock**.","The Sync button in the side menu opens a quick list of sources with a coloured dot: green is fine, orange is waiting, red failed."]}
  ]},

  "set.data":{title:"About Import and export",lead:"Bring payments in from a file, or take your data out. Everything lives on your own server.",blocks:[
    {h:"What this tab is for",p:["If a bank is not connected, or you want older history, you can import a CSV file. You can also export your data any time."]},
    {h:"Import",p:["**Import Wise CSV** adds a Wise statement. **Choose CSV file** adds a bank or card export: first pick the **Account** it belongs to.","Turn on **Charges are positive numbers** if your card file lists spending as plus numbers.","Rows already imported are skipped. Rows that match payments you typed by hand are merged. Nothing is doubled."],ex:"Import a 2-year-old statement: only the payments you do not have yet are added."},
    {h:"Pension and sync",p:["**Update pension balance** is where you type your pension. It is entered by hand.","**Sync now** reads all connected sources right away."]},
    {h:"Currencies",p:["The shekel is always the display currency. You can **Add** other currencies you hold. Rates come from the European Central Bank each day.","A currency stays as long as an account holds it. A currency without an account has an **×** to remove it."]},
    {h:"Export",p:["**Export…** opens a window: what to export, the period, categories, accounts, type, text, tag, which extra items to include (transfers, card bill payments, upcoming) and the columns. You see a preview, then choose **CSV** (opens in Excel or Sheets) or **JSON**.","The file is created on this device. Nothing is sent anywhere."]},
    {h:"Full backup",p:["**Download backup** saves everything in one JSON file. Your data is also in the nightly backup of your server."]}
  ]},

  "set.alr":{title:"About Which alerts",lead:"Choose which kinds of alerts you want, and how sensitive they are.",blocks:[
    {h:"What this tab is for",p:["Not everyone wants every alert. Here you switch each kind on or off. The alerts you get appear on the Alerts page and at the top of Home."]},
    {h:"Which alerts to show",p:["One switch for each kind: payments that look like they came from a jar, bills due or overdue, bill price changes, budget limits, a card charge much higher than last month, large transactions, transfers and duplicates to review, balances that do not match the bank, a source that is out of date, uncategorized transactions, a forecast that turns negative, and income without documents.","Turn a switch off and that kind stops showing, and stops being sent."],demo:"alert"},
    {h:"The amount under a switch",p:["**Card charge higher by (%)**: warn when a card this month is more than this percent above last month. Starts at 10.","**Large transaction from (₪)**: warn about any payment this big in the last 7 days. Starts at ₪5,000.","**Bill reminder (days before)**: warn this many days before a bill. Starts at 3.","**Budget warning at (%)**: warn when a budget is this much used. Starts at 80."],ex:"Budget warning at 80, Groceries ₪2,600: you are warned at ₪2,080."},
    {h:"Most urgent first",p:["Alerts are sorted by how urgent they are. An overdue bill or a budget that is already over comes first. A bill due soon or a budget at its warning level is next. Price changes, large payments and uncategorized items come last."],ex:"**Netflix looks overdue** shows above **12 transactions need a category**."},
    {h:"Dismissed by mistake",p:["**Show dismissed alerts again** brings back alerts you hid. **Go to alerts →** opens the page.","Where alerts are sent is in the Notifications tab."]}
  ]},

  "set.notify":{title:"About where alerts go",lead:"Choose where alerts are sent when you are not looking at the app: your phone, Telegram, or another service.",blocks:[
    {h:"What this tab is for",p:["Alerts always show inside the app. Here you can also get them outside it. When the app is closed, the server sends them to the places you turn on below."]},
    {h:"On this device",p:["The line **Permission** shows if this browser may show notifications. **Allow notifications** asks the browser. **Send a test** shows one right away so you know it works.","Notifications show while the app is open on this device."]},
    {h:"ntfy",p:["ntfy is a free notification service you can run on your own server. Type your topic address and press **Send test to ntfy**. Optional."]},
    {h:"Telegram",p:["Alerts come as Telegram messages. Create a bot with @BotFather and paste its **Bot token**. Then add your **Chat id**: send a message to your bot and look at the getUpdates page.","Press **Save**. The status turns **On**. **Send a test** checks it. **Remove** turns it off."]},
    {h:"Webhook",p:["A webhook sends alerts to Discord, Slack, Home Assistant, n8n and similar. Paste the **Webhook address** and press **Save**. Use **Send a test** and **Remove** the same way."]},
    {h:"Privacy",p:["Telegram and webhooks send the alert text, with account names and amounts, over the internet to that service. Turn them on only if you are fine with that.","Which kinds of alerts are sent is set in the Which alerts tab."],tip:"WhatsApp has no free official way to message yourself. A Telegram bot or a webhook does the same job."}
  ]},

  "set.sec":{title:"About password and sign-in",lead:"Protect your app: your password, an extra code from your phone, and where you are signed in.",blocks:[
    {h:"What this tab is for",p:["This app holds private money data. These settings decide who can open it."]},
    {h:"Password",p:["Type your **Current password** and a **New password** with at least 10 characters, then press **Change password**.","Changing it signs out every other device."],ex:"Use a long sentence you can remember, not a short word."},
    {h:"Recovery key",p:["A one-time key that lets you choose a new password if you forget it. It is shown when you first choose the password, and only then: use **Copy**, **Download** or **Print** and keep it somewhere safe, away from this device.","Press **Make a new recovery key** and type your password to get a new one. The old one stops working at once."],tip:"Anyone who has the key can choose a new password, so keep it like a house key."},
    {h:"Forgot the password",p:["On the sign-in screen press **Forgot password?**. Then choose **I have my recovery key**, or **Send a code to my phone** (shown only when alerts reach your phone: Settings → Where alerts go). The code works for 10 minutes.","Choose a new password. With two-step sign-in on, the code from the authenticator app is asked too. Every device is signed out, and an alert says the password was changed.","After using the recovery key you get a new one: save it too.","Neither works? On Docker run **docker compose exec app node src/cli.js set-password**. On the Windows or Linux app, install it fresh and restore a backup."]},
    {h:"Two-step sign-in",p:["This adds a 6-digit code from your phone each time you sign in, so a stolen password is not enough.","Press **Set up**. You see a key. Add it to an authenticator app (Aegis, Google Authenticator, 1Password), enter the 6-digit code and press **Turn on**.","To switch it off, type your password and press **Turn off**."],tip:"Save the key somewhere safe. If you lose both your phone and the key, you may not be able to sign in."},
    {h:"Good habits",p:["Use a password you use nowhere else. Turn on two-step sign-in. Press **Sign out everywhere** if you ever lose a device.","The app can only read your accounts, so even someone who gets in cannot move your money. They could still see your data, which is why these settings matter."]},
    {h:"Signed-in devices",p:["You stay signed in on a device for 14 days.","**Sign out** only signs out this device. **Sign out everywhere** signs out all devices, including this one."]}
  ]},

  "set.app":{title:"About Version and updates",lead:"Check which version you run, update it, and install the app on your phone or computer like a normal app.",blocks:[
    {h:"What this tab is for",p:["Two cards: one for versions and updates, one for installing the app on a device."]},
    {h:"Version and updates",p:["**Installed version** shows what you run. **What's new** lists what changed.","The Windows app keeps itself up to date: it shows **Download and update** and then **Restart and update**. There is also **Update automatically**: new versions install the next time you close the app.","If you run the app on your own server, it only tells you that a newer version exists. To update, run the two shown commands in the project folder. Your data is kept."],tip:"**Check for updates** needs internet access to github.com."},
    {h:"Install this app",p:["Installing opens the app full screen from your home screen and lets it open without a connection.","Press **Install app** if the button shows. Otherwise: on Android or desktop Chrome, use the browser menu and choose Install app. On iPhone, tap Share, then Add to Home Screen.","The steps for this device come first. **Other devices** lists the rest, with the apps you can download for Windows, Mac, Linux and Android. iPhone and iPad have no app to download: add it to the Home Screen."]},
    {h:"What's new",p:["**What's new** next to the version number opens a short list of what changed in each release, in plain words."]},
    {h:"Offline support",p:["**Offline support** says if the app can open without internet. It needs to be opened once over HTTPS first. When offline, a banner says you are seeing saved data."]}
  ]},

  "set.log":{title:"About Change history",lead:"A diary of everything that changed in the app: by you, and by the app itself. Use it to find out what happened, or to undo a mistake.",blocks:[
    {h:"What this tab is for",p:["Every change is written here, newest first: a category you changed, a budget, a jar, a bill that was found, jars paid automatically, and more."]},
    {h:"Reading a line",p:["Each line has what happened, the details, who did it (**You** or **System**), and the time."],ex:"Edited category - Pharmacy: Uncategorized → Health - You - 3 Oct, 14:02."},
    {h:"What is recorded",p:["Things you do (adding a transaction, changing a category, editing a jar or budget) and things the app does on its own (finding a bill, paying from a jar, returning a payment to a jar).","Nothing here changes your real bank. It is only a record inside the app."],ex:"**Bill detected** - Netflix, monthly, about ₪55 - System."},
    {h:"Undo",p:["Some lines have an **Undo** button. Edits to categories, notes, budgets and jars can be undone. Press it and the old value comes back."]},
    {h:"More lines",p:["The list shows 50 at a time. Press **Show 50 more** to go further."]}
  ]},

  appearance:{title:"About Appearance",lead:"Make the app look the way you like. Every change shows right away and is saved in this browser only, so each device can look different. **Reset** (top right) brings back the defaults.",blocks:[
    {h:"Mode",p:["**Light**, **Dark** or **Auto**. Auto follows your phone or computer setting."]},
    {h:"Colours",p:["Pick a **colour palette**. Choose **Custom** to make your own: pick one base colour and the rest follow, or set each colour yourself. You edit the colours of the mode you are in (Light or Dark)."]},
    {h:"Backdrop",p:["**Background**: ten styles, from **Glow** and **Mesh** to **Aurora**, **Horizon**, **Two-tone**, **Corner glow** and **Sweep**, or **Flat** (no effect). **Gradient strength** makes the colour softer or stronger.","**Texture** puts a light pattern on top: **None**, **Dots**, **Stripes**, **Grid** or **Static**. **Texture density** makes the pattern bigger or smaller, and **Texture opacity** makes it fainter or stronger."]},
    {h:"Surface",p:["How cards look: **Solid**, **Outline**, **Raised** or **Glass**.","**Glass** lets the background show through every card, window and menu. Three sliders appear: **Blur** (how blurred the background looks through them), **Vibrance** (how bright and colourful it looks) and **Opacity** (how solid the card colour is: 100% hides the background, 0% shows it fully). The background itself does not change. If the app feels slow, go back to **Solid**."]},
    {h:"Corners",p:["**Round**, **Soft** or **Sharp** corners on cards and buttons."]},
    {h:"Density and spacing",p:["They are two different things. **Density** (Compact, Cozy, Roomy) changes the space inside cards and rows. **Spacing** (Tight, Standard, Loose, Wide) changes the gap between cards and sections.","On a computer, **Sidebar spacing** (Tight, Standard, Roomy) changes the gap between side-menu items."],ex:"Compact density with Wide spacing: small cards that are far apart."},
    {h:"Font and navigation",p:["**Font**: **Sans**, **Serif**, **Rounded** or **Mono**.","On a computer, **Navigation** chooses **Labels** (icon and name) or **Icons only** (a thin menu)."]},
    {h:"App icon and language",p:["**App icon** is the symbol in the round logo: Shekel, Dollar, Euro, Pound, Yen or Coin.","**Language**: **English** or Hebrew (עברית). Hebrew also flips the page to right-to-left.","Tip: click the logo at the top of the side menu for a random new look."]}
  ]},

  quick:{title:"About the + button",lead:"The + button is a quick way to add or update things from any page. Press it, pick what you want to do, and fill the short form.",blocks:[
    {h:"What the + button is for",p:["You do not need to find the right page first. It is the round + button in the corner of the screen (in the middle of the bottom bar on a phone). The window is called **Add or update**."]},
    {h:"Transaction",p:["**Transaction** adds an income or an expense by hand. Fill in **Description**, **Amount**, **Type** (Expense or Income), **Date**, **Account** (or Cash) and **Category**. **Auto (by rules)** lets your category rules choose. You can attach a **Receipt**.","If the account is one you keep by hand, you can tick **Also change this account's balance by this amount**."],ex:"Pharmacy, ₪48, Expense, today, Max ·· 1234."},
    {h:"Receipt photo",p:["**Receipt photo** opens the same form and straight away opens your camera or your files. Take the photo and add the details. The photo is saved with the transaction."]},
    {h:"Category rule and category",p:["**Category rule** makes a rule: when a transaction name contains your text, it gets the category you pick. It never changes a category you set by hand.","**Category** creates a new category by name."],ex:"If the description contains \"Wolt\", category Eating out."},
    {h:"Bill, budget, jar and goal",p:["**Bill** tracks a recurring charge. **Budget** sets a monthly limit for a category. **Jar** makes a savings pot (a deadline is optional). **Goal** makes a jar with an amount to reach.","Each opens the same form as on its own page."]},
    {h:"Pension, import and sync",p:["**Pension balance** updates your pension by hand. **Import a CSV** takes you to Settings → Import and export. **Sync now** reads all connected accounts."]}
  ]}
};

HELP["set.prof"]={title:"About Profile",lead:"Your profile is a few details about you. Every one is optional, and none of them leaves your own data.",blocks:[
  {h:"What the profile is for",p:["The **name** is used for the greeting on Home. The **age** lets you set goals such as a sum by a certain age. The **gender** lets the app speak to you correctly in Hebrew, where words change for women and men.","Press **Save** to keep your changes. **Clear profile** removes all of it."],ex:"Name Dana, age 34, gender female: Home says **Good morning, Dana**, and in Hebrew speaks to you in the feminine."},
  {h:"The first-time window",p:["The first time you open the app after this was added, a window offers the same form. **Not now** closes it for good. You can fill the profile in here at any time."]}
]};

HELP.recap={title:"About Recap",lead:"Recap tells you, in plain words, how your current month is going. You do not have to look anything up: it reads your data and writes the story.",blocks:[
  {h:"What Recap is for",p:["It answers the questions you would otherwise look up in several pages: what came in, what is still to be paid, what you spent, which budgets are in trouble, and where the month is heading.","It only says what is true for you right now. A sentence that does not apply is simply not shown."],ex:"**Hi Dana, here is your October so far.** You got paid ₪18,900 on 9 October. You have ₪6,200 of bills and card payments still ahead."},
  {h:"The row of days",p:["Under your name is the month as a row of small bars, one for each day. Hover a day to see what came in, what was spent and what is planned for it. Click a day to open it in Activity."]},
  {h:"The steps",p:["The page follows your money in order: what you **began** the month with, what **came in**, what you **spent**, what you are **left with** today, what you **still have to pay**, anything **worth a look** (a budget going over, jars that will be short, a category above its usual), and the **likely end** of the month.","Each step shows the sum that gets you from one number to the next, so you can see how it was worked out. Tap a step's title to open the page with the full details."]},
  {h:"Credit cards",p:["A credit card purchase counts as spent the day you make it, even though the bank pays the card company later, on the card's charge day. Until then it shows as **not taken yet**, and it is part of **still to pay**.","A card that takes the money at once, like a Wise card, counts like any payment from your account. When the card's charge shows up in your bank, it is no longer owed. This all works by itself from your transactions."]},
  {h:"Where the numbers come from",p:["**You began with** is an estimate: your balance today, minus what came in this month, plus what already left your accounts.","**Likely end** is what you have today minus your credit card bills, the bills still due and the rest of your usual spending (your budgets, or what you usually spend where there is no budget). It assumes no more income arrives.","In the last days of the month it also shows the bills likely due next month."],tip:"Tap a step's title to go to the page with the full details."}
]};
HELP["set.ai"]={title:"About Automatic sorting",lead:"These sections sort your payments for you: they give them a category, tags, a clearer name, or mark card bills and say what money coming in is. A category or name you set by hand is never changed.",blocks:[
  {h:"Let an AI make your categories",p:["The app comes with only the few categories it needs itself. **Let an AI make your categories** builds the rest from your own transactions: download the file with your transaction names, copy the instructions into any AI chat and attach the file, then upload the answer.","Before anything is added you see what it adds, and you can uncheck categories you do not want. Nothing you already have is changed, entries you sorted yourself keep their category, and Undo works as usual.","The file has only the names (shops and payers), how often each appears, and whether money went out or came in. No amounts, dates or accounts. It does go to the AI company you choose."]},
  {h:"Category rules",p:["A rule says: if the transaction name contains this text, use this category. The first rule that matches wins. A category you set by hand is never changed by a rule.","To add one, type the text, choose a category and press **Add rule**. Edit the text or category of existing rules in place, or press **Delete**."],demo:"rule",ex:"If the description contains \"shufersal\", the category is Groceries."},
  {h:"Where a rule looks",p:["Every rule reads: **If** [where] [how] [text] → [what it does]. The first list says where it looks that says where it looks for the text: **Everything**, or one part of the entry, such as **Transaction name**, **Bank's note** (extra text from the bank), **Who paid**, **Paid to**, **Your note**, **Your account**, **Bank's category** or **Currency paid in** (like USD).","Each kind of rule starts with the places it always read, for example **Name, from or to** for category rules. The second list says how the text is compared: **contains**, **is exactly**, **starts with**, **ends with** or **does not contain**. Your rules keep matching what they matched before (with **contains**) until you change this. The change is in the change history and can be undone."],ex:"If Bank's note contains \"acme ltd\" → Salary."},
  {h:"Tag rules",p:["A tag rule works like a category rule, but it adds one or more tags. It adds them on top of the category.","When you add a rule, the app can also tag the payments you already have. A rule needs at least one tag."],ex:"\"netflix\" adds the tag \"streaming\"."},
  {h:"Display names",p:["A display name rule gives entries a clearer name. Only what you see changes: the bank's text, your rules and reports still use the original.","Choose where to look (**Everything**, **Transaction name**, **Bank's note** and so on), **contains** or **is exactly**, the text, and the name to show."],ex:"If Bank's note contains \"Acme Ltd\" → Salary."},
  {h:"Card payments",p:["A bank line that contains the text is the bill of a credit card. It is not counted as spending, because each purchase is already counted on the card.","The usual card companies are recognised with no rule."],ex:"\"ישראכרט חיוב\" → Card payment."},
  {h:"Money coming in",p:["Money coming in that holds the text (in the transaction name, the payer or the bank's note) is what you pick: **Salary** or **Money back**. Your choice on one payment comes first.","With no rule: money that came in on a credit card is Money back, and all other money coming in is Income. Nothing is decided from words in the text.","A rule changes no category: salary and money back are not categories."],ex:"\"wix\" → Salary. \"insurer\" → Money back."}
]};
for (const k of ["crules", "trules", "nrules", "cprules", "srules"]) HELP["set." + k] = HELP["set.ai"];
export default HELP;
